sha256":"sha256:05aa4997f11d3bfd421c1f4224faa2215df99f57085ff135cc5882c477dc0a49","file":"preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":36,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"42947810192fd66c3a8a7a9ec8fd2df8f20c7e15a44c1dc8ec413f62ceeaa08d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:05aa4997f11d3bfd421c1f4224faa2215df99f57085ff135cc5882c477dc0a49","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Randomized-quasipolynomial-time-mean-payoff-games-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex#L36"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a uniform randomized algorithm that, for every such game,\nreturns the entire set\n\\[\n U=\\{v\\in V:\\text{there is a Max strategy }\\sigma\n       \\text{ such that for every Min strategy }\\tau,\\ \n       \\operatorname{MP}_w(\\pi_{v,\\sigma,\\tau})\\ge0\\}\n\\]\ncorrectly with probability at least $7/8$.\nFor an absolute constant $C>0$, on every random tape its total cost is at\nmost\n\\[\n 2^{C(\\log_2(L+2))^2}\n\\]\nbit operations in a standard model polynomially equivalent to a uniform\nprobabilistic Turing machine. The bound includes preprocessing, recursive\ncalls, intermediate arithmetic, and random-bit generation."}
